# pycore rule
- Python 3.10+, ASCII-only code/output. All imports at file top (stdlib → third-party → internal); never inside functions/try. Absolute imports only.
- No try/except in AI-written code except where spec allows (file/network, queue, Tk lifecycle); else use conditional checks / error-status return / ColorPrint.
- Third-party only via `pycore.pyfoundations.third_party` getters (e.g. `get_third_package_torch()`), never direct `import torch`; register in third_party.py.
- Layers: pyfoundations = stdlib only; pyutils = third-party OK, exports singletons; pyctl orchestrates; constants via `from pycore.pygvar import X`. Cache/tmp from pygvar (CACHE_DIR/TMP_DIR); static files in root `public`.
- Singletons (i18n, bus_manager) are module-level globals, never instance vars. i18n: `from pycore.pyutils.native_ui.step0_i18n import i18n`; launcher calls `i18n.extend_translations(...)` before `i18n.get()`; no hardcoded UI strings, no `i18n.get(key, default)`.
- Threading: components subclass `threading.Thread` (name ends "Thread"); communicate via THREAD_BUS. Forbidden: ThreadPoolExecutor, Timer, Queue-module, manual locks, thread-local, lambda in Thread/`root.after`, cross-thread callbacks. Tk only from Tk thread.
- Heartbeat (pycore/pyfoundations/heartbeat/): direct Thread inherit, hard-coded registry.py, TaskModel+TaskHandler, IDLE/PROCESSING/ERROR/DISABLED, no locks/async/dynamic-registration, single heartbeat thread.
- DB (pycore/database/): table keys via `TableKeys`, namespaces via `TableNamespaces` (`common`/`app_{n}`/`util_{n}`); no hardcoded table names.
- MCP (pycore/pyutils/mcp/, pyapps/mcp/): no ColorPrint (breaks JSON-RPC); stdlib logging only; tools `async`, return `Dict` w/ `success`, never raise; STDOUT=JSON-RPC/STDERR=logs; `PYCORE_MCP_MODE=1`; `ensure_stdio_has_buffer_attributes()` before FastMCP import.
- Apps (pyapps): entry `{appname}_main.py` w/ start()/main(); subdirs `{appname}_{config,i18n,bus_keys}`+controller/service/routes/model/scripts; `register_bus_keys()` first in start().
- Misc: OCR via `pycore.pyutils.ocr.ocr_manager` (CnOCR). RPC via `pycore.pyutils.rpc.UnifiedRpcServer`, WebSocket-first. WebView (PySide6) bg color set in `<head>` before CSS to avoid FOUC. Module Caller: port 59000, `python3 -m pycore.callmodule`, GUI needs `PYUTILS_LOAD_GUI=1`.
